          "created": "2026-09-18T18:31:44.000Z",
          "id": 1240991,
          "npm_advisory_id": null,
          "overview": "http-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons.",
          "reported_by": null,
          "title": "http-cache-semantics max-stale handling can disclose cross-user cached responses",
